.TH GIT-MOVE 1
.SH NAME
git-move \- reorder a commit without opening an editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git move
<commit> --before=<commit>
.br
.B git move
<commit> --after=<commit>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Move a commit immediately before or after another commit, keeping it as a
separate commit. Commit arguments accept hashes or Git refs.
Both commits must be ancestors of HEAD. The history being replayed must
contain no merges. Tracked files must have no staged or unstaged changes.
Reordering rewrites commit hashes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --before=<commit>
Place the source immediately before the target.
.TP
.B --after=<commit>
Place the source immediately after the target.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
git move HEAD --before=HEAD~2
git move abc1234 --after=def5678
git-move HEAD~2 --after=HEAD
.fi
.SH CONFLICTS
Resolve conflicts, stage the resolved files, then run
.BR "git rebase --continue" .
To cancel and restore the original history, run
.BR "git rebase --abort" .
